        A system built around trust,
        rather than control.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="section-body">
      <p class="large-copy">
        The project began with the assumption that safety in an
        isolated environment would require monitoring. It ended with
        a more careful question: how little monitoring can a community
        rely on while still feeling supported?
      </p>

      <p>
        The final direction prioritised transparency, consent,
        minimal data collection and user control. Safety remained
        important, but it was reframed as something created through
        social structures and responsible interaction rather than
        constant observation.
