        What made this project valuable was that the most important
        decisions were not only about usability or visual design.
        They were about responsibility. Every additional piece of
        information the system could collect created another question
        about privacy, power and trust.
      </p>

      <p>
        Working across physical products, digital interfaces and
        community rules made me think about experience design as more
        than a sequence of screens. The behaviour of the entire system
        matters — including the parts a user may never directly see.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>


